{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_1","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"pwd && rg --files -g 'source.txt' -g 'AGENTS.md' -g 'rewritten.txt' && cat source.txt\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_1","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"pwd && rg --files -g 'source.txt' -g 'AGENTS.md' -g 'rewritten.txt' && cat source.txt\"","aggregated_output":"/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-kalepail-Desktop-kalepail-skills/fd5aae97-76bc-4bb3-8597-af0fa91bb3f0/scratchpad/probe-runs/sol-high__prose__r1__1791297197/work\nsource.txt\nWhen the fleet daemon was upgraded to v4.12.0 last quarter, the routing table that had previously been stored in several scattered files was consolidated into a single file at /etc/fleetd/routes.toml, which is read once at startup and then cached in memory until the process is restarted or a reload signal is received from the supervisor. Operators who were accustomed to editing the old files directly were advised that any change should first be validated by running the reload command with the --dry-run flag, because a malformed entry that was not caught before the reload would cause every worker in the pool to fall back to the default route, and that fallback was found during the incident review to cost roughly $0.35 per thousand requests in extra upstream charges. The reload command prints a diff of the routes that would change, and it exits with a nonzero status if any entry cannot be parsed, so it can be wired into a pre-commit hook without much effort. Older entries that were written for the previous schema were automatically migrated, but entries that referenced retired regions were dropped and logged as warnings.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_2","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"python3 - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport re\n\nsource = Path('source.txt')\noriginal = source.read_bytes()\ntext = ('The fleet daemon upgrade to v4.12.0 occurred last quarter. '\n        'The routing table previously occupied several scattered files. '\n        'The upgrade consolidated the routing table into one file at /etc/fleetd/routes.toml. '\n        'The daemon reads this file once at startup and caches it in memory. '\n        'It keeps this cache until the process restarts or the supervisor sends a reload signal. '\n        'Operators accustomed to editing the old files directly received advice to validate every change before reloading. '\n        'They should first run the reload command with the --dry-run flag. '\n        'If no one detects a malformed entry before reload, every worker in the pool falls back to the default route. '\n        'The incident review found that this fallback adds roughly \"'$0.35 in upstream charges per thousand requests. '\"'\n        'The reload command prints a comparison showing which routes would change. '\n        'It exits with a nonzero status if it cannot parse any entry. '\n        'These features let operators add the command to a pre-commit hook with little effort. '\n        'The system automatically migrated older entries from the previous schema. '\n        'However, the system dropped entries that referenced retired regions and logged them as warnings.\\\\n')\nsentences = [s.strip() for s in re.split(r'[.\"'!?]'\"', text) if s.strip()]\ncounts = [len(s.split()) for s in sentences]\nassert max(counts) <= 20, counts\nassert not re.search(r'\\\\b(?:was|were|been)\\\\s+(?:\\\\w+ly\\\\s+)?\\\\w+ed\\\\b', text, re.I)\nfor token in ['/etc/fleetd/routes.toml', '--dry-run', 'v4.12.0', '\"'$0.35'\"']:\n    assert token in text\nassert source.read_bytes() == original\nPath('rewritten.txt').write_text(text)\nassert source.read_bytes() == original\nprint('Saved rewritten.txt. All rule checks passed. Maximum sentence length:', max(counts))\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
